WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:15.216
The saved Week 17 plan identifies a high-acuity multisystem medical capstone and a trauma capstone with multiple mechanisms and diagnostic mimics. It does not include the actual examination cases or answer key.
已保存的第17周计划要求练习高急度多系统内科综合案例，以及包含多重机制和诊断模拟因素的创伤综合案例，但未提供正式考题或答案。

00:00:15.216 --> 00:00:27.960
The following scenarios are newly written practice examples. They train prioritization, alternatives, reassessment, PCR and handover; they are not predictions of the school examination.
以下情景为全新原创练习案例，训练优先级、替代解释、复评、PCR和交接；它们不是对学校考试内容的预测。

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:45.144
The patient has sudden breathlessness, weakness and new confusion. A family member reports a change from baseline, and a medication list is present. No single diagnosis is supplied; the crew must identify urgent threats and gather relevant evidence.
患者突然出现呼吸困难、虚弱和新发意识混乱。家属报告患者较基线发生变化，并提供用药清单。案例没有给出单一诊断；团队需要识别紧急威胁并收集相关证据。

00:00:45.144 --> 00:00:58.920
Begin with immediate safety and primary threats. Obtain focused history and measurements using authorized equipment, verify unexpected signals and request the clinical support required by the current pathway.
应从即时安全和主要威胁开始。使用获准设备采集重点病史和测量值，核实异常信号，并按照现行流程请求所需临床支援。

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:14.664
Do not anchor on a single alarming symptom. Consider respiratory, circulatory, metabolic, neurologic and medication-related possibilities as categories, then use the patient’s actual findings and current pathway to narrow them.
不要被单一显著症状锚定。可将呼吸、循环、代谢、神经和药物相关问题作为候选类别，再根据患者实际发现及现行流程缩小范围。

00:01:14.664 --> 00:01:28.848
If altered mental status is part of the case, use the school-taught assessment sequence and check for reversible contributors when the current pathway calls for it. State what you know, what you do not know and what should be reassessed.
如果案例包含意识改变，应遵循学校教授的评估顺序，并在现行流程要求时检查可逆因素。应说明已知信息、未知信息以及需要复评的内容。

00:01:28.848 --> 00:01:42.624
The patient is found after a fall, with visible bruising, confusion and reported new weakness. The witness did not see the full sequence; the patient’s medication card and chronic-disease history are available.
患者跌倒后被发现，出现可见瘀伤、意识混乱并被报告有新发虚弱。目击者没有看到全过程；现场有患者药物卡和慢性病史。

00:01:42.624 --> 00:01:57.480
Treat the injury as real while asking whether a medical event could have caused or contributed to the fall. Protect immediate threats, obtain the event timeline and avoid dismissing a serious injury because another explanation also fits.
应把损伤视为真实问题，同时询问是否有内科事件导致或促成跌倒。先保护即时威胁，查明事件时间线；即使存在其他解释，也不能因此忽视严重损伤。

00:01:57.480 --> 00:02:12.384
A diagnostic mimic is a reason to widen the assessment, not a reason to stop assessing trauma. Preserve the mechanism, any unknown interval, observed injuries, patient trend and relevant history as separate facts.
诊断模拟因素意味着要拓宽评估，而不是停止创伤评估。应将受伤机制、未知时段、所见损伤、患者趋势和相关病史分别记录为事实。

00:02:12.384 --> 00:02:26.472
Use the school’s current trauma and medical approach. Do not choose an advanced intervention or treatment from this practice vignette; stay within PCP authorization and escalate when the patient or mechanism warrants it.
应使用学校现行创伤与内科处理方法。不要根据本练习案例选择高级干预或治疗；应遵守PCP授权，并在患者情况或受伤机制要求时升级处置。

00:02:26.472 --> 00:02:37.584
For either case, chart the source and time of each important cue. Keep the witness account, patient account, objective findings and crew interpretation separate.
两个案例都应注明重要线索的来源和时间。目击者陈述、患者陈述、客观发现和团队解释要分别记录。

00:02:37.584 --> 00:02:51.696
The written record and SBAR/MIST handover should tell a consistent story. Include uncertainty, the trend and the immediate next concern instead of presenting a false sense of diagnostic certainty.
书面记录和SBAR/MIST交接应保持叙述一致。应包括不确定性、变化趋势和下一项紧急关注，而不要假装诊断已完全确定。

00:02:51.696 --> 00:03:03.048
The saved school plan calls for a student-led seven-question debrief. These original prompts organize that reflection; they are not presented as the school’s verbatim seven questions.
已保存的学校计划要求学生主导七问复盘。本原创问题用于组织反思，并非学校官方七个问题的逐字内容。

00:03:03.048 --> 00:03:15.720
Keep the debrief psychologically safe and evidence-based. Describe decisions and conditions rather than labeling the learner; end with one narrow drill and a way to observe the next attempt.
复盘应兼顾心理安全和证据。描述决策及当时条件，不给学习者贴标签；最后选定一项聚焦练习和一种观察下一次表现的方法。

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:39.744
Make the medical case concrete. The adult is confused and breathing hard, with glucose two point seven millimoles per litre, room-air saturation eighty-eight percent, breathing twenty-eight and pressure eighty-eight over fifty-six. These are fictional observations for reasoning, not a new clinical cutoff set. Check measurement quality while addressing the immediate patient threats.
把内科案例具体化：成人意识混乱、呼吸费力，血糖2.7毫摩尔每升，室内空气饱和度88%，呼吸28，血压88/56。它们是推理练习的虚构观察值，不是一套新增临床阈值。应在处理即时患者威胁的同时核实测量质量。

00:03:39.744 --> 00:04:06.336
Low glucose is a treatable finding, but it does not explain away impaired oxygenation or poor circulation. Protect the airway and provide the indicated respiratory support while arranging the authorized glucose correction. If the person cannot safely follow instructions and swallow, do not put an oral treatment into an unprotected airway. Seek the support the patient needs rather than waiting for a perfect diagnosis.
低血糖是可处理的发现，但不能借此抹去氧合及循环问题。保护气道并提供有指征呼吸支持，同时安排获准血糖纠正。若患者不能安全遵令及吞咽，不可将口服治疗放入未受保护气道。应寻求患者需要的支持，而不是等待完美诊断。

00:04:06.336 --> 00:04:31.128
For the next simulation cue, stipulate that an appropriately authorized clinician has completed indicated glucose treatment and respiratory support. Repeat glucose is five point one, saturation ninety-five with support and pressure one hundred two over sixty-four. The patient is more attentive, but breathing is still laboured. Report both the change and what did not improve.
下一条模拟线索设定为：适当获准人员已完成有指征的血糖处理及呼吸支持。复测血糖5.1，支持下饱和度95%，血压102/64。患者注意力改善，但呼吸仍费力。应同时报告已改变及未改善之处。

00:04:31.128 --> 00:04:57.816
Reassess the airway, work of breathing, circulation, neurologic findings and the measurement context. Ask about recent illness, intake and medication use without assuming an overdose from a medication list. Ongoing acute illness means this is not a simple recovered low-glucose release example. Continue indicated care and time-sensitive conveyance, with clinical advice when needed.
复评气道、呼吸做功、循环、神经发现及测量背景。询问近期疾病、进食及用药，但不能仅凭药物清单认定过量。仍有急性病情，就不是单纯低血糖恢复后的留置现场示例。应继续有指征照护及时间敏感转运，需要时寻求临床建议。

00:04:57.816 --> 00:05:20.760
A useful situation statement is: this adult remains acutely breathless after correction of confirmed low glucose. Then give the sudden change, relevant medication history, initial findings, actual actions and repeat findings. Say that saturation improved with respiratory support; do not present it as an untreated room-air value.
有用的Situation表述是：这位成人确诊低血糖纠正后仍急性呼吸困难。再说明突然变化、相关用药、初始发现、真实处置及复测发现。必须说明饱和度是在呼吸支持下改善，不可写成未经处理的室内空气读数。

00:05:20.760 --> 00:06:19.968
An original handover using situation, background, assessment and recommendation. Situation: an adult remains acutely breathless after treatment of confirmed low glucose. Background: family reports a sudden change and provides the insulin list; the complete cause is not established. Assessment: initial glucose two point seven millimoles per litre, saturation eighty-eight percent on room air, respiratory rate twenty-eight and pressure eighty-eight over fifty-six. Repeat glucose five point one, saturation ninety-five percent with support and pressure one hundred two over sixty-four, but breathing remains laboured. Recommendation: urgent receiving-team assessment of the unresolved respiratory and circulatory problem, with ongoing monitoring and support. Include actual treatment details and times; these fictional values are not a destination algorithm.
原创SBAR示例，按Situation、Background、Assessment及Recommendation组织。Situation，成人确诊低血糖处理后仍急性呼吸困难。Background，家属报告突然变化并提供胰岛素清单，完整病因尚未确定。Assessment，初始血糖2.7毫摩尔每升、室内空气饱和度88%、呼吸28、血压88/56；复测血糖5.1，支持下饱和度95%、血压102/64，但呼吸仍费力。Recommendation，请接收团队紧急评估未解决的呼吸及循环问题，并继续监护支持。需补充真实处置细节及时间；这些虚构数值不是目的地算法。

00:06:19.968 --> 00:06:43.584
In the trauma example, a witness last saw the adult at usual function at thirteen forty-five, then found the patient near the stairs at fourteen twelve. Confusion and left-sided weakness persist. Glucose is six point two, and the medication history includes an anticoagulant. Keep the two times, direct findings and reported history separate.
创伤示例中，目击者最后于13:45看到成人处于正常功能状态，14:12在楼梯附近发现患者。意识混乱及左侧无力持续，血糖6.2，药物史含抗凝药。必须区分两个时间、直接发现及所报告病史。

00:06:43.584 --> 00:07:08.304
There is a real injury concern and a possible preceding neurologic or other medical event. A normal glucose value does not prove stroke; a visible bruise does not explain every neurologic finding. Obtain the relevant focused assessment, protect immediate threats and seek the appropriate time-sensitive trauma and neurologic pathway advice without delaying care for a complete story.
既有真实损伤担忧，也可能有先于跌倒的神经或其他内科事件。正常血糖不证明卒中，可见瘀伤也不能解释所有神经发现。应作相关重点评估、保护即时威胁，并寻求适当且时间敏感的创伤及神经路径建议，不能为了查全故事延误照护。

00:07:08.304 --> 00:07:33.144
Continue the actual trauma assessment: address airway or breathing compromise and significant bleeding, preserve perfusion and use the indicated movement and spinal-protection approach. Do not apply an adult low-risk clearance rule as if an altered patient with weakness met every requirement. Reassess neurologic findings rather than documenting only the first examination.
继续真实创伤评估：处理气道呼吸障碍及显著出血、保护灌注，并采用有指征的移动及脊柱保护方法。不能假定意识改变且无力的患者满足成人低风险排除规则的全部条件。应重复神经评估，而不是只记录首次检查。

00:07:33.144 --> 00:07:55.608
The anticoagulant history increases the importance of communicating possible bleeding risk, but does not establish the site of bleeding or authorize a reversal medicine. Do not turn the practice case into permission for an advanced intervention. Report the uncertain sequence, persistent deficit, treatment response and destination concern to the appropriate clinical team.
抗凝药史使可能出血风险更需要明确沟通，但不能据此确定出血部位，也不授权逆转药。不能将练习案例变为实施高级干预的许可。应向适当临床团队报告不确定事件先后、持续缺损、处置反应及目的地担忧。

00:07:55.608 --> 00:08:15.816
A useful mechanism statement preserves both the incomplete fall account and the possibility of a preceding event. Distinguish observed bruising from suspected head or spinal injury. Include the focal weakness, confusion, glucose and any subsequent changes, and state the actual treatments and response.
有用的Mechanism表述应同时保留不完整跌倒经过及可能先发事件。区分所见瘀伤与怀疑的头部或脊柱损伤，报告局灶无力、意识混乱、血糖及随后变化，再陈述真实处置和反应。

00:08:15.816 --> 00:09:11.160
An original handover using mechanism, injuries, signs and treatment. Mechanism: found near stairs at fourteen twelve after an incompletely witnessed fall; last observed at usual function at thirteen forty-five. Injuries: visible bruising and possible head or neck injury, with the complete injury pattern still under assessment. Signs: confusion and persistent left-sided weakness; capillary glucose six point two millimoles per litre, not a demonstrated low-glucose explanation. Treatment: report the actual airway, bleeding, movement-protection and monitoring actions and the response, not an assumed treatment bundle. Highlight anticoagulant history, the uncertain sequence and the need for time-sensitive destination advice. Do not label the case proven ischemic stroke or merely a mechanical fall.
原创MIST示例，按Mechanism、Injuries、Signs及Treatment组织。Mechanism，14:12在楼梯附近跌倒后被发现，目击过程不完整；13:45最后观察到正常功能。Injuries，可见瘀伤及可能头部或颈部损伤，完整伤情仍在评估。Signs，意识混乱及持续左侧无力，毛细血管血糖6.2毫摩尔每升，未证明低血糖能解释表现。Treatment，报告实际气道、止血、移动保护和监护措施及反应，而非假定的一整套处置。强调抗凝病史、不确定的事件先后，以及时间敏感的目的地咨询需要。不能将其写成已确诊缺血性卒中或单纯机械性跌倒。

00:09:11.160 --> 00:09:36.912
Use this five-part practice plan for the school five-minute documentation target, not as a mandatory operational time limit. First establish the event and evidence sources. Add focused assessment and relevant history, then the actual actions and times. Finish the response, current concern and accepted handover before checking units, missing times and unsupported conclusions.
可用这五部分计划练习学校五分钟记录目标，但它不是强制操作时限。先建立事件与证据来源，再写重点评估及相关病史，然后记录真实行动及时间。完成反应、当前担忧和已接受交接，再检查单位、缺失时间及无依据结论。

00:09:36.912 --> 00:09:56.616
Never invent a treatment time, examination finding, consent discussion or successful handover to fill the form. Mark a fact as unknown when it is unknown, and distinguish later information from what drove the earlier decision. Necessary patient care takes priority over finishing a practice timer.
不能为了填表而编造处置时间、检查发现、同意讨论或成功交接。不知道的事实应标明未知，并区分后获信息与早先决策依据。必要患者照护优先于完成练习计时。

00:09:56.616 --> 00:10:18.792
In the medical case, ask whether the learner noticed persistent respiratory effort after glucose improved. In the trauma case, ask whether the learner separated last-known-well from discovery time and kept both injury and medical causes in view. These are observable decisions, not personality judgments or a self-awarded examination pass.
内科案例应检查学习者是否注意到血糖改善后仍持续的呼吸费力。创伤案例应检查其是否区分最后正常与发现时间，并同时保留损伤和内科病因。它们是可观察决定，不是人格评价，也不是自授考试及格。

00:10:18.792 --> 00:10:40.296
Change one cue for the next repetition: for example, the witness cannot confirm the last normal time, or a repeat measurement is unreliable. Explain how that changes the plan and handover. The goal is transfer of reasoning under changed evidence, not memorization of these two fictional patients.
下一轮可改一个线索，例如目击者不能确认最后正常时间，或复测读数不可靠。解释计划及交接应如何改变。目标是在证据改变时迁移推理，而不是背下这两个虚构患者。
